pk('R1','review','P0','REVIEWER 1: tracks V and T (interpreter, loader, shims)', ['gpu/hwcodec/review/r1/**'], ['every DONE post of track V/T'],
   ['For each package that posts DONE: read the code against its package entry and the frozen header; run its run_tests.sh (build in /tmp/n2hw-r1); look specifically for: semantics that deviate from the ARM ARM (flag computation, PC bias, IT handling, writeback order, sign/zero extension, saturation, NaN/rounding), tests that mirror the implementation, unbounded loops/recursion on guest-controlled input, host pointer leaks into guest memory, thread-safety of shared tables, guest-pointer validation in shims. Write independent spot tests for at least 10 instruction forms per class package (your own literals).',
    'Post each finding to the owner and hw-lead: file:line, what is wrong, a failing input, the expected result with its source. Keep review/r1/FINDINGS.md (id, package, severity, status open/fixed/rejected). Re-check fixes. You never edit other packages\' files.'],
   'Your spot tests are the oracle; cross-check doubtful instruction semantics by assembling with llvm-mc and reasoning from the ARM ARM pseudocode, and with T01\'s differential harness.',
   ['review/r1/FINDINGS.md lists every package of V and T with a verdict (accept / accept with findings / reject) before the 5-hour mark'], 'none', ['all hw-v*','hw-t01','hw-iv','hw-lead'], role='reviewer')
pk('R2','review','P0','REVIEWER 2: kernel code, JPEG, daemon/protocol, plug-ins, rule compliance', ['gpu/hwcodec/review/r2/**'], ['every DONE post of tracks K, J, P, D'],
   ['Kernel code first (it can hang or corrupt the phone): every register write against the cited Linux source line and against gpu/hwcodec/kernel/b/bsd/dev/nord2_hwcodec.inc; every wait bounded; no access to a block before its domain is on and unprotected; only this driver\'s bits written in shared registers (SPM, infracfg protection, topckgen mux, larb ports); user pointers and sizes validated before copyin/copyout; integer overflow in size computations; locking; behaviour on close and on a killed client; physical ranges inside the claims of include/redwood_vcodec.h. Then protocol/daemon robustness (malformed messages, timeouts), plug-in ABI conformance with gpu/video/include/n2vt_abi.h, FACTS.md evidence quality.',
    'Rule compliance sweep every 45 minutes: `find gpu/hwcodec -type f -size +300k`, binaries in the tree, files outside owned paths (git status), missing SPDX lines, vendor code pasted; post violations to the owner and hw-lead.',
    'Findings as for R1 in review/r2/FINDINGS.md.'],
   'The Linux sources and the phone-verified model are the oracle for kernel code.',
   ['review/r2/FINDINGS.md lists every package of K, J, P, D with a verdict before the 5-hour mark; a kernel package without your "accept" is not handed to the main session'], 'none', ['hw-k01','hw-k02','hw-ik','hw-j02','hw-j04','hw-ip','hw-p03','hw-p04','hw-d01','hw-lead'], role='reviewer')

ids=[p['id'] for p in P]; assert len(ids)==len(set(ids))
